§§ `68(c) — the supplement for a parent paid an Income Support benefit or a maintenance payment`

-- src:826 | (ג) הורה שמשתלמים לו בעד חודש מסוים גמלה לפי חוק הבטחת הכנסה או תשלום חודשי לפי חוק המזונות (הבטחת תשלום), התשל״ב–1972, והוא זכאי בעד אותו חודש לקצבת ילדים כאמור בסעיפים קטנים (א) או (ב) בעד שלושה ילדים או יותר, תיווסף לקצבת הילדים המשתלמת לו בעד הילד השלישי ובעד הילד הרביעי שבמנין ילדיו תוספת בסכום השווה ל־70% מן הסכום הבסיסי הקבוע בפסקה (2)(ג) שבהגדרה ”הסכום הבסיסי“.
@ref National Insurance Law s 68(c) (source line 826)
GIVEN `the person`                IS A `A person`
      `the number of children`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(c) applies to` `the person` `, entitled for this number of children:` `the number of children` MEANS
        (    "גמלה לפי חוק הבטחת הכנסה" ... `the person`'s `paid, for the month, a benefit under the Income Support Law`
         OR  "תשלום חודשי לפי חוק המזונות (הבטחת תשלום)" ... `the person`'s `paid, for the month, a monthly payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law`)
    AND "בעד שלושה ילדים או יותר" ... `the number of children` AT LEAST 3

-- "a supplement equal to 70% of the basic amount fixed in paragraph (2)(c)", for "the third
-- child and the fourth child in his count".
@ref National Insurance Law s 68(c) (source line 826); s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (2)(c) (source line 189)
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 68(c) — the supplement, before rounding, at` `the amounts` MEANS
    70% TIMES `the basic amount for a supplement under section 68(c), under` `the amounts`

@ref National Insurance Law s 68(c) (source line 826)
GIVEN `the place` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(c) — the supplement is added for the child at place` `the place` MEANS
        "בעד הילד השלישי" ... `the place` EQUALS 3
    OR  "ובעד הילד הרביעי" ... `the place` EQUALS 4

§§ `Section 68 — one child's line`

@ref National Insurance Law s 68(a)-(c) (source lines 821-826)
GIVEN `the amounts`                 IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
      `section 68(c) applies`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the child`                   IS A `A child`
GIVETH A `The allowance for a child in the count`
`s 68 — the allowance for a child in the count` `the amounts` `section 68(c) applies` `the place` `the child` MEANS
    `The allowance for a child in the count` WITH
        `name of the child`                                          IS `the child`'s `name`
        `place in the count`                                         IS `the place`
        `the provision`                                              IS `the provision`
        `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b), before rounding`  IS `s 68 — the monthly allowance, before rounding, under` `the provision` `, at` `the amounts`
        `the supplement under section 68(c), before rounding`        IS `the supplement`
    WHERE
        `the provision`  MEANS `s 68 — the provision that fixes the allowance for the child at place` `the place` `:` `the child`
        `the supplement` MEANS
            IF       `section 68(c) applies`
                 AND `s 68(c) — the supplement is added for the child at place` `the place`
            THEN `s 68(c) — the supplement, before rounding, at` `the amounts`
            ELSE 0

§§ `Section 68 — a person's child allowance for the month`

-- s 66 first: a person who is not an insured parent, or is one with income chargeable to
-- additional tax, has no allowance. Otherwise one line per child in the person's count (s 67), in the
-- count's order; no children is an allowance with no lines. (0.2.0: asked of the day or the month.)
@ref National Insurance Law ss 66, 67, 68 (source lines 813-826)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`, `the readings` IS A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
      `the family`  IS A `A family on a day`, `the amounts` IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
      `the person`  IS A `A person`
GIVETH A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
`s 68 — the child allowance, asked` `the question` `, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` `, of` `the person` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the deposited text of sections 65 to 68 was in force on` (`the family`'s `the day`)
           THEN `this model answers days from 1 May 2015, when sections 1 and 68 took their present wording; the text in force before then is not in its sources`
           IF NOT `s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` (`the readings`'s `for a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`) `:` `the person`
           THEN `no child allowance, not being an insured parent`
           IF `s 66 — an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax, reading a resident housewife as` (`the readings`'s `for a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`) `:` `the person`
           THEN `no child allowance, being an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax`
           OTHERWISE `a monthly child allowance` `the lines`
    WHERE
        `the count`     MEANS `s 67 — the count of children, asked` `the question` `, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, of` `the person`
        `the number`    MEANS count `the count`
        `with (c)`      MEANS `s 68(c) applies, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, to` `the person` `, entitled for this number of children:` `the number`
        `the places`    MEANS zip (range 1 `the number`) `the count`
        `the lines`     MEANS map `the line for` `the places`
        `the line for` pc MEANS
            `s 68 — the allowance for a child in the count` `the amounts` `with (c)` (pc's fst) (pc's snd)

-- The month's total for one person: the allowance and any supplement, before rounding.
-- A person with no allowance has a total of nothing, which is 0 shekels.
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total, before rounding, of` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `a monthly child allowance` `the lines`
    THEN sum (map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b), before rounding` PLUS l's `the supplement under section 68(c), before rounding`) `the lines`)
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `Section 68 — the day's forms, and the month's (versions 0.2.0 and 0.3.0)`

-- `s 68 — the child allowance, asked …` above answers the question it is asked (nii-il06-nouns.l4,
-- `The question asked of a family on a day`) at the readings of forks F18 and F2 it is given
-- (version 0.3.0; nii-s65-interpretation.l4). The form by the name of version 0.1.0 answers the
-- day at the readings the switches name; the form with `, reading` takes the readings the caller
-- names. The month's takes `A family in a month`: its count is the children s 72 pays for in the
-- month that s 67 places with the person (fork F19), and s 68(c)'s "entitled for that month … for
-- three or more children" is read on that count. The lines cited elsewhere (43-49, 156-159) hold
-- the rules they held before 0.2.0.

@ref National Insurance Law ss 66, 67, 68 (source lines 813-826)
GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
      `the family`   IS A `A family on a day`
      `the amounts`  IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
      `the person`   IS A `A person`
GIVETH A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
`s 68 — the child allowance, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` `, of` `the person` MEANS
    `the answer to` (GIVEN r YIELD `s 68 — the child allowance, asked` `the allowance on the family's day` `, reading` r `, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` `, of` `the person`)
        `at` `the readings` `, in` `the family`
        `, two answers merged by` (GIVEN x, y YIELD `one answer for a person from two readings:` x `and` y)

@ref National Insurance Law ss 66, 67, 68 (source lines 813-826); forks F18, F2
GIVEN `the family`  IS A `A family on a day`
      `the amounts` IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
      `the person`  IS A `A person`
GIVETH A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
`s 68 — the child allowance, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` `, of` `the person` MEANS
    `s 68 — the child allowance, reading` `the readings this row takes where the text does not decide` `, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` `, of` `the person`

@ref National Insurance Law ss 66, 67, 68 (source lines 813-826), s 72(a) (source line 854); forks F18, F2
GIVEN `the family`  IS A `A family in a month`
      `the amounts` IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
      `the person`  IS A `A person`
GIVETH A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
`s 68 — the child allowance for the month, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` `, of` `the person` MEANS
    `the answer to` (GIVEN r YIELD `s 68 — the child allowance, asked` `the allowance for the month of the family's day, for the children section 72 pays for in it`
                                       `, reading` r `, in` `the day's family` `, at` `the amounts` `, of` `the person`)
        `at` `the readings this row takes where the text does not decide` `, in` `the day's family`
        `, two answers merged by` (GIVEN x, y YIELD `one answer for a person from two readings:` x `and` y)
    WHERE
        `the day's family` MEANS `the family in a month, on its day:` `the family`

-- Two answers for one person, at the two other readings of a declined fork, as one (version 0.3.0):
-- the same answer; or, where neither pays anything (no allowance, or an allowance with no child in
-- the count), that no allowance is payable on either reading; otherwise none, and the question is
-- declined. Only fork F18 can give two such answers that differ in kind: fork F2 moves a child into
-- or out of a count, never whether a person is insured.
@ref forks F18 and F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN x IS A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
      y IS A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
GIVETH A MAYBE `The child allowance of a person for the month`
`one answer for a person from two readings:` x `and` y MEANS
    BRANCH IF x EQUALS y
           THEN JUST x
           IF `nothing is payable under` x AND `nothing is payable under` y
           THEN JUST `no child allowance on either reading of whether this person is insured, which section 65 does not decide`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`nothing is payable under` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `a monthly child allowance` `the lines` THEN null `the lines`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `68(c) at fork F14 (version 0.4.0)`

-- "a parent to whom is paid for a given month a benefit under the Income Support Law or a monthly
-- payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law, and who is entitled for that month to
-- the child allowance … for three or more children". Fork F14, ruled by Meng on 2026-10-08
-- (SHRUG): where the parent paid is not the parent in whose count the children are, the text does
-- not say whether the supplement is added (switch and refusal in nii-s65-interpretation.l4).
-- Readings: only where the parent whose count it is is paid (this row's in 0.1.0 to 0.3.0); or
-- where any person of the family is paid. Declined by default where the two differ.
@ref National Insurance Law s 68(c) (source line 826); fork F14 (ruled by Meng, 2026-10-08, SHRUG)
GIVEN `the readings`           IS A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
      `the family`             IS A `A family on a day`
      `the person`             IS A `A person`
      `the number of children` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(c) applies, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, to` `the person` `, entitled for this number of children:` `the number of children` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the readings`'s `for the supplement where another parent is paid`
    WHEN `the supplement is added only where the parent whose count it is is paid` THEN `only this parent`
    WHEN `the supplement is added where any person of the family is paid`          THEN `any person`
    WHEN `a case that turns on which parent is paid is declined`
    THEN IF   `only this parent` EQUALS `any person`
         THEN `only this parent`
         ELSE `section 68(c) does not say whether the supplement is added where the parent paid an Income Support benefit or a maintenance payment is not the parent whose count it is`
    WHERE
        `only this parent` MEANS `s 68(c) applies to` `the person` `, entitled for this number of children:` `the number of children`
        `any person` MEANS
                any (GIVEN p YIELD     p's `paid, for the month, a benefit under the Income Support Law`
                                   OR  p's `paid, for the month, a monthly payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law`)
                    (`the family`'s `the persons`)
            AND "בעד שלושה ילדים או יותר" ... `the number of children` AT LEAST 3
